  "prefLabel": "Rev 3201.05 First come-first served basis",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rev 3201.05 “First come-first served basis” means the method by which the department processes education tax credit applications by the day submitted, where more than one application received on a specific day will be processed on a random basis before moving on to the next day’s applications.\n\nSource. #10236, eff 11-28-12; ss by #13462, eff 10-13-22 (formerly Rev 3201.08) (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Rev 3200)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/rev3200.html"
